  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>&nbsp;long metal rod <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi><mi>Y</mi></math> completes the circuit as shown in figure. The plane of the circuit is perpendicular to the magnetic field of flux density <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>. If the resistance of the circuit is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8486;</mo></math>, the force needed to move the rod in direction, as indicated, with a constant speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> will be _______<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0034_b7ceda218135.png\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 157px;\" /></p><p>&nbsp;</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "18",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The force on the rod is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>B</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>B</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>l</mi><mi>B</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>v</mi></mrow><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>The data given is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace></math></p><p>Substituting the values in equation (i)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
}